  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a spherical shell of radius R at temperature T. The black body radiation inside it can be considered as an ideal gas of photons with internal energy per unit volume <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math> and pressure <math><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> . If the shell now undergoes an adiabatic expansion the relation between T and R is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>T</mi><mo>&prop;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>T</mi><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>T</mi><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>T</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
